  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-10-22T13:47:03.456Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When a shader meant for Quest is used on the PC build of an avatar, all sorts of strange subtle things go wrong in-world, mostly related to shadows and transparency -- but in the editor, everything seems fine.  So more than once I've accidentally published a build of the PC version of an avatar while it still had its mobile material set (from having just uploaded its mobile version).  I know there are tools that will help automatically swap and so on, but one very simple built-in approach would just be to have a warning in the validations, pointing out that using mobile standard in a PC build will produce glitchy results (like how the inverse situation is already prevented due to PC shaders being strictly forbidden on mobile).",
